<title>
Rear Wheel House Outer Panel and Rear Wheel House Outer Extension (Partial) or Rear Wheel House Outer Extension Removal and Installation
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
The figure below shows condition where the following parts are removed.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Front fender 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLBA0C9A06005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Quarter-pillar outer panel 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLBA0C9B06016"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Fuel filler door panel 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLBA0C9806017"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFBA0A9B0157.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "131.476mm" ver = "01" gw = "455" gh = "356"/>
</figure>
<servinfosub id = "AENLBA0C9B06017001">
<title>
General Notes
</title>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Welding method and number of welding points are the same on both sides. This repair instruction shows procedure for left side.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
If side sill strength is installed to the body, replace rear wheel house outer extension partially.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
If side sill strength is removed from the body, replace rear wheel house outer extension.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLBA0C9B06017002">
<title>
Removal
</title>
